=20
> have to use more complicated mechanisms for that, like {da poi su'o mei=
=20
> cu simxu lo ka prami} (which isn't *that* bad).=20
>
>
No, because the domain of {da} of {da poi (ke'a) su'o (re) mei} spans=20
distributively over plural {su'o (re) mei}_1.=20
{da poi ke'a gunma cu simxu lo ka prami} treats the plural {simxu}_1=20
collectively,
just like a developed form of {su'o loi}=3D{su'o da poi ke'a me lo gunma be=
=20
lo}.

=20


